# Workspace objectives and linked work

When workspace **aim** or **objectives** change, always run `reconcile_objective_links` on `study_design` **before persisting**. Never leave orphan `objectiveIds` in plan steps or `findingLinks`.

## Where links live

- `methodsPlan.steps[].objectiveIds`, `analysisPlan.steps[].objectiveIds`
- `objectiveLinks.findingLinks[].objectiveIds`
- Optional future: `projectTasks[].linkId`, per-objective `tasks[]`

Valid link targets: `"aim"` ([AIM_LINK_ID](apps/web/lib/objectives.ts)) and current objective UUIDs from `workspaces.objectives`.

## Reconciliation (required)

Shared helpers (keep Python and TS in sync):

- Server: [objectives.py](services/peggy-api/core/objectives.py) or [study_design_merge.py](services/peggy-api/core/study_design_merge.py) — `reconcile_objective_links(study_design, valid_ids, reassign_map?)`
- Client preview: [studyDesign.ts](apps/web/lib/studyDesign.ts) — same behaviour before Save

On workspace PATCH when objective IDs are removed:

1. Compare before/after objective IDs.
2. If user chose reassign in the confirm dialog, apply `reassign_map` first.
3. Strip any remaining unknown IDs from all link arrays above.
4. Persist reconciled `study_design` in the same request (server-side authority).

Do **not** rely on client-only pruning. [pruneFindingLinks](apps/web/lib/studyDesign.ts) handles deleted **papers** only; objective deletion needs `reconcile_objective_links`.

## UX when removing an objective with links

Confirm dialog: show affected plan steps, findings, and tasks. User picks **reassign** or **unlink**. Empty objectives delete without prompt.

## Docs

When adding or changing objective lifecycle, tasks, or link shapes, update [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) and [docs/DATABASE.md](docs/DATABASE.md) per [docs.mdc](.cursor/rules/docs.mdc).
